            "review_text": "maryyeo\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam4531 contributions\n0\nHits and Misses, overall pretty average\nSep 2020\nHits:\n- Visited the outlet in the new Crescent Mall wing. The ambience was rather inviting with comfortable cushioned seats.\n- The menu was impressive with a variety of rather authentic-looking Thai dishes, and with the chef being touted as a famous chef in Thailand. (not sure, maybe?)\n- The service staff was polite and attentive.\n- The Tom Yum soup was rather prettily displayed in a mini brass-looking hotpot, and had cute little big-headed and roundish octopus that I don't see in other mainstream Thai restaurants.\n\nMisses:\n- The Tom Yum soup had the right note of spiciness and tanginess, but probably could use slightly stronger-tasting herbs e.g. more lemongrass to make it closer to Thailand's. Also, the ingredients appeared a little miserly - exactly two small octopus, two small prawns, two small slices of fish, two half-pieces of mushrooms. Each item was about 2 centimeters in size. We understand there are costs concerns, but the lack of ingredients really made the soup sad-looking and a little unappealing.\n- The pomelo salad was warm (heated up). Almost all Thai restaurants we've tried both in Singapore and in Vietnam served this dish cold. So we ain't sure why...?\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten October 14, 2020",
